  "note": "A Div two Bdes up with a reserve Bde withdrawing by night (OOW3 2006 s2-s12). The Div covering troops an Armd Regt or its subunits with artillery, engineers, LAT and mot infantry, held forward to the time Corps sets (s6 para 12 p 32). The click is the Div HQ of the old posn; the aim is the way of withdrawal, the second click the new defensive posn (planned). Laid on OOW3 Annex P (p 75): rear parties left by each forward Bde (s9 para 5 p 45); the Bdes back on their own axes to the clear line, several axes to avoid congestion and the En air, the routes converging from the outer flanks protected (s2 para 5 a p 8); covering troops delaying in front of each intermediate posn (s6 paras 9-13 pp 31-32); a flank guard on the threatened flank if required (para 24 p 34); two intermediate posns, each held by a complete formation under one Comd with more fire in front and less depth (paras 16-22 pp 33-34), each far enough beyond the one before that the En must re-deploy his field artillery (p 33; IBB p 373: the En 105 mm IFG 17.2 km, ORBAT); the reserve Bde the reserve (s7 para 5 p 40); the primary demolition belt continuous across the new posn's front (s12 para 5 a p 56); the BL close to own troops and moved back often (p 67). Timings in the Annex A pattern (pp 72-73). Posns are drawn turned to face the En behind the plan. GSP 1947 Inf Div in Battle s30 (pp 141-151) agrees on the covering troops (elms of the Armd Regt and / or the LAT Bn with some artillery, engineers and infantry, para 9 b p 143), the flank guard (on LAT Bn elms, para 11 p 144), the intermediate posns (strong enough to make the En deploy his main force, far enough apart that he must move his artillery, held by the fewest troops, paras 14-15 pp 144-145) and the timings (para 21 p 147). Two points differ: the book would leave out the intermediate posns when the covering troops can do the job, to save infantry (para 15 p 145), and normally the Div Comd details a reserve Bde to prepare and occupy the rear main posn (para 17 p 145), where OOW3 s7 pp 39-40 prefers fresh troops, else a portion of the force, and keeps the reserve (a Bde at the least) for counter-attacks; this layout follows OOW3 (the depth Bde the reserve, the new main posn drawn planned).",
